# Sepet Kod Denetimi

Bu denetim "'`sepet/` altındaki Python backend modulleri, `schema.sql`, frontend kaynak dosyalari, stiller, Vite/TypeScript yapilandirmalari ve README uzerinde yapildi. Derleme cikislari (`web/dist/*`), lockfile ve ikili `sepet.db` dosyasi davranis analizi icin ayri olarak degerlendirilmedi.

## 1. Module map

| Module | Responsibility | Reads | Writes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `sepet/api/db.py` | SQLite connection factory, UTC timestamp, password hashing/verification. | None directly. | None directly. |
| `sepet/api/auth.py` | Bearer token resolution and role/profile guards for customer, restaurant and courier. | `auth_token`, `user`, `restaurant`, `courier`. | None. |
| `sepet/api/accounts.py` | Registration, login, current-user lookup and customer wallet top-up. | `user`. | `user`, `restaurant`, `auth_token`. |
| `sepet/api/main.py` | FastAPI composition, restaurant browsing and customer order creation/detail. | `restaurant`, `restaurant_review`, `menu_item`, `user`, `order`, `order_item`. | `user`, `order`, `order_item`. |
| `sepet/api/panels.py` | Customer history, restaurant operations, courier assignment/delivery, delivery confirmation and earnings. | `order`, `restaurant`, `user`, `courier`, `order_item`, `menu_item`. | `order`, `courier`, `user`, `menu_item`. |
| `sepet/api/reviews.py` | Eligibility check, creation of restaurant reviews and display-rating helper. | `restaurant`, `order`, `restaurant_review`. | `restaurant_review`. |
| `sepet/api/seed.py` | Deletes/recreates SQLite file and loads demo restaurants, menus, users and couriers. | `restaurant`; reads `schema.sql`. | `restaurant`, `menu_item`, `user`, `courier`. |

## 2. Coupling

All backend modules share the same `sepet.db` file through `db.get_db()` (`sepet/api/db.py:8`, `sepet/api/db.py:11-14`), so table responsibilities are only by convention, not enforced by an isolated data-access layer.

| Dependent module | Dependency | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| `main.py` | `accounts` router | import `sepet/api/main.py:7`; registration `sepet/api/main.py:15` |
| `main.py` | `auth` authorization helpers | import `sepet/api/main.py:8`; optional user guard `sepet/api/main.py:83`; customer guard `sepet/api/main.py:143` |
| `main.py` | `db.get_db()` | import `sepet/api/main.py:9`; calls `sepet/api/main.py:47`, `75`, `84`, `121`, `149` |
| `main.py` | `panels` router | import `sepet/api/main.py:10`; registration `sepet/api/main.py:16` |
| `main.py` | `reviews.displayed_rating()` and router | import `sepet/api/main.py:11`; calls `sepet/api/main.py:59`, `103`; registration `sepet/api/main.py:17` |
| `accounts.py` | `auth.get_current_user` | import `sepet/api/accounts.py:7`; protected endpoints `sepet/api/accounts.py:102`, `111` |
| `accounts.py` | `db` helpers | import `sepet/api/accounts.py:8`; token insert uses `utc_now()` `sepet/api/accounts.py:54`; password hash `sepet/api/accounts.py:67`; DB calls `sepet/api/accounts.py:62`, `91`, `115`; password verify `sepet/api/accounts.py:95` |
| `auth.py` | `db.get_db()` | import `sepet/api/auth.py:3`; calls `sepet/api/auth.py:19`, `42`, `54` |
| `panels.py` | `auth` guards | import `sepet/api/panels.py:6`; customer `sepet/api/panels.py:69`, `227`; restaurant `sepet/api/panels.py:87`, `107`, `129`, `149`, `164`, `248`; courier `sepet/api/panels.py:191`, `208` |
| `panels.py` | `db` helpers | import `sepet/api/panels.py:7`; DB calls `sepet/api/panels.py:70`, `101`, `109`, `120`, `133`, `151`, `168`, `193`, `211`, `229`, `250`; password hash `sepet/api/panels.py:138`; timestamps `sepet/api/panels.py:167`, `210`, `228` |
| `reviews.py` | `auth.require_customer` | import `sepet/api/reviews.py:5`; guard `sepet/api/reviews.py:22` |
| `reviews.py` | `db` helpers | import `sepet/api/reviews.py:6`; DB calls `sepet/api/reviews.py:26`; timestamp `sepet/api/reviews.py:48` |
| `reviews.py` | `panels.ReviewInput` | import `sepet/api/reviews.py:7`; request model `sepet/api/reviews.py:21` |
| `seed.py` | `db` helpers | import `sepet/api/seed.py:4`; password hash `sepet/api/seed.py:193`; timestamp `sepet/api/seed.py:194` |

A notable circular-adjacent dependency exists: `reviews.py` imports its request model from `panels.py` (`sepet/api/reviews.py:7`), while `main.py` imports both routers (`sepet/api/main.py:10-11`). This is harmless at runtime but couples a review request schema to panel route code.

## 3. Request lifecycle

All handlers resolve through `db.get_db()` (`sepet/api/db.py:11-14`) and use `sqlite3.Row` rows. FastAPI dependency functions are named explicitly below.

| Endpoint | Handler | Path to database and back |
|---|---|---|
| `POST /api/auth/register` | `accounts.register()` (`sepet/api/accounts.py:59`) | `validate_registration()` (`:61`) -> `get_db()` (`:62`) -> reads `user` (`:63`) -> writes `user` (`:65-68`) and optionally `restaurant` (`:70-84`) -> `issue_token()` writes `auth_token` (`:85`, `50-56`) -> transaction commit -> token/user response (`:86`). |
| `POST /api/auth/login` | `accounts.login()` (`sepet/api/accounts.py:89`) | `get_db()` (`:91`) -> reads `user` (`:92-94`) -> `verify_password()` from `db.py` (`:95`) -> `issue_token()` writes `auth_token` (`:97`) -> user payload (`:98`). |
| `GET /api/auth/me` | `accounts.me()` (`sepet/api/accounts.py:101`) | `Depends(get_current_user)` -> `resolve_user()` (`sepet/api/auth.py:18`) -> `_user_from_token()` reads `auth_token JOIN user` (`:10-15`) -> `get_current_user()` enforces presence (`:23-26`) -> `user_payload()` (`sepet/api/accounts.py:31-32`). |
| `POST /api/auth/wallet/topup` | `accounts.top_up_wallet()` (`sepet/api/accounts.py:110`) | `get_current_user` -> `resolve_user` -> `_user_from_token` (`sepet/api/auth.py:10-15`) -> role check (`:112-113`) -> `get_db()` (`:115`) -> updates `user.balance` (`:116-119`) -> reselects balance (`:122`) -> response (`:123`). |
